---
/** D15. /guides/best-fantasy-manhwa — see src/components/BestManhwa.astro. */
export const prerender = true
import BestManhwa from '../../components/BestManhwa.astro'
---

<BestManhwa
  slug="best-fantasy-manhwa"
  genre="Fantasy"
  keywords={['best fantasy manhwa', 'fantasy manhwa', 'best fantasy webtoons', 'fantasy manhwa to read', 'top fantasy manhwa']}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Fantasy is the biggest genre in manhwa and the widest. It covers game-like worlds with status windows and
      levels, reincarnation into a novel the hero once read, sword-and-sorcery kingdoms, and the romance fantasy
      that fills the palace and duchy stories. Many of the most-read manhwa of the last ten years started as web
      novels in this genre.
    </p>
    <p>
      This list keeps to fantasy manhwa you can read on an official platform, ranked by what readers scored them.
      Each title links to its page, with every official platform and how much of it is free.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Reading fantasy manhwa on the official apps</h2>
  <p>
    Fantasy is spread across every app. WEBTOON and Tapas carry many of the long-running adventure series, and
    Tappytoon, Lezhin and Manta hold a large share of the licensed romance fantasy. A lot of fantasy manhwa are
    adapted from web novels, and the original novel is often published officially too. It is usually far ahead of
    the comic, if you cannot wait for the next chapter.
  </p>
</BestManhwa>
